                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm an original Kickstarter backer and have been waiting patiently for this game to be finished.  The backer alpha that you are able to buy here on Steam Early Access looks nothing like the game you will be getting when/if it ever is complete.\n\nThe dev decided to, without even running it past the original Kickstarter backers to see what we thought, to change the graphical style of the game to super-low resolution textures and sprites instead of 3d objects.  The fidelity of the game is now what Daggerfall is.  Lars promised us a game that looked like Oblivion (even better in some cases) and has now arbitrarily downgraded to Daggerfall.  I love Daggerfall, don't get me wrong, its a good game because of the massive amount of content in it.  It was revolutionary when it was released in the mid-1990s.  It is also painfully ugly (and was even when it was released).  FRONTIERS will not be the content monster that Daggerfall was.\n\nThe developer even spent the better part of a year porting the game over from Unity 4 to Unity 5, and touted VR support as a major benefit of the move to the new engine.  But that's gotta be gone now too, because who would want to play Daggerfall in VR?\n\nEssentially, the game ran poorly in the Alpha version you can play here on Steam, so to try to cheer us up with move to nightmarishly awful visuals, the dev says that with the significantly reduced graphical fidelity, the game will run much better.  Thanks for making it look like crap.  It's true that gameplay is far more important than graphics, however in this case that philosophy is stretched to the point of breaking.\n\nIt's been almost 5 whole years since I backed this project, and every year it gets worse.  This actually isn't progress.  The game is at a worse point that it was 3 years ago.  All of the art assets that looked pretty good have all been thrown out, and replaced with sloppily made generic as can be pixel art.  All of the textures in the game had to redone.  The 3D models (already pretty low poly to begin with) have had their polys reduced.  The dev needs to remove the deceptive screenshots before someone gets fooled and buys something that is this significantly different.",
